SECTION | KEY | VALUE
----------------------------------------
# tuning.pdl - the numbers of rpg-space that get changed often (milliseconds unless noted). Edit, no rebuild: the daemon re-reads this file whenever its size or modified time changes (checked every reload_ms).
# TUNE | name | value | what it does                                                              (a missing or bad row falls back to the built-in default shown in the last column)
# Both front ends read this file: the old toys-menu window (rpg-space.xhtpm) and the pc-hq board window (board/pchq-board.xhtpm); the daemon (ops/rpg_space.c) is the one program behind both. See TWO-CODEBASES.md.
# --- CPU safety (house hq-cpu-safety.md): raising these lowers CPU, lowering them makes the window react sooner ---
TUNE | reload_ms       | 2000  | how often the static data (catalog, party, rooms, door pages) and this file are re-read                         | 2000
TUNE | flag_cache_ms   | 150   | how long a flag / switch read is reused inside the daemon                                                       | 150
TUNE | follow_ms       | 400   | at most how often the board's rooms are exported and the engine woken when nothing changed                      | 400
TUNE | viewer_scan_ms  | 2000  | how often /proc is scanned for an open rpg-space / board window (no window = nothing is rendered)                 | 2000
TUNE | far_repaint_ms  | 1500  | a pet stepping in a room nobody watches repaints the scene at most this often                                   | 1500
TUNE | greet_page_ms   | 6000  | at most one events-hq greeting page per this long (each costs ~150 ms of CPU); the built-in text covers the rest | 6000
# --- game feel ---
TUNE | step_min_ms     | 1500  | a pet walks on its own (INT off) every step_min_ms + a random 0..step_jitter_ms                                 | 900
TUNE | step_jitter_ms  | 900   | the random part of that                                                                                         | 700
# --- board window input ---
TUNE | edge_poll_ms    | 400   | how often the daemon looks at the board's Interact state (an In: click from the pc-hq key turns INT on)         | 400
TUNE | engage_retry_ms | 20000 | INT on: how long to wait before sending the engine's Interact key a second time (it is a toggle: keep this long) | 20000
TUNE | click_poll_ms   | 150   | how often a click on the board's 2D canvas is looked at (a click on a pet or the trainer selects them)          | 150
# rpg-space (16 pets on a 56-wide island page): fewer, bigger output bursts. out_min_ms = at most one render + ui.txt write per this many ms (the pets still step on their own timers)
TUNE | out_min_ms       | 250   | at most one scene / ui write per this many ms (0 = after every pet step, the old behaviour of the other pets games) | 0
TUNE | direct_max       | 16    | how many cells the planet may slide away under the ship in DIRECT flight (0..16; the map is the planet page and its eight neighbour pages, 48 x 48)                                                 | 16
TUNE | map_box          | 1     | 1 = draw a grey box at the limit of the planet map under the ship (outer ring grey, four tall corner pillars): shows where the map ends while the planet slides away in direct flight (tests and presentations)  | 1
TUNE | ship_alt         | 2     | height of the ship piece above the planet page in direct flight (cells)                                                                                      | 2
TUNE | ship_start_x     | 6     | where the ship piece starts on the planet page                                                                                                                | 6
TUNE | ship_start_y     | 6     | where the ship piece starts on the planet page                                                                                                                | 6
TUNE | remnant_z       | 17    | the world level remnant blocks lie on: the ship floor is level 16, characters stand at 17 (the hero piece's own pos_z resets after a reload, do not use it)                                                  | 17
TUNE | direct_z_min     | -8    | the lowest ship altitude in DIRECT flight (collision.pdl contact_alt is -7: below it the hull is in the land)                                                  | -8
TUNE | direct_z_max     | 12    | the highest ship altitude in DIRECT flight                                                  | 12
TUNE | obj_reach        | 2     | how far from the hull rectangle (desk cells) the mining beam reaches an asteroid of the PLANET MAP in direct flight (design 7i)                                  | 2
TUNE | obj_top          | 6     | ship altitude at or below which the hull cannot pass over an asteroid or another ship of the planet map (above it the ship flies over)                          | 6
TUNE | obj_draw        | 1     | asteroids and other ships of the planet map: 1 = voxel pieces the engine draws (pieces/veh_N), 0 = the old flat tiles painted into the page                    | 0 1
TUNE | rock_vox_min    | 5     | fewest voxels in an asteroid nugget                                                                                                                         | 1 40
TUNE | rock_vox_max    | 11    | most voxels in an asteroid nugget                                                                                                                           | 1 40
TUNE | obj_vox_pct     | 100   | size of one voxel of those pieces in percent of a desk cell                                                                                                 | 25 400
TUNE | obj_z           | 1     | height of the underside of the voxel pieces over the land at ship altitude 0 (cells, positive only: tune() ignores 0 and below, absent = 0); MEASURED: the Bridge floor top is at 1 (a cube with its underside at 1 rests on it, at 0 is buried); the planet surface vs ship altitude is NOT measured | 0
TUNE | scene_flat      | 0     | 1 = remnants and resource nodes in a room are the old flat sprite rows again; 0 (default) = voxel pieces (loot bag, nugget; pieces/veh_10..24)                  | 0 1
TUNE | node_cell_pct    | 150   | width of a resource node's voxel nugget in percent of a cell (a remnant's bag is blocks.pdl PICKUP size)                                                     | 50 300
TUNE | bar_radius      | 48    | the bottom bar lists every ship and asteroid of the planet map within this many cells of the ship (Chebyshev, from the hull centre); 16 = the whole 48 x 48 land   | 48
TUNE | space_all_desks | 1    | the asteroids and the other ship (pieces veh_1..9) are drawn on EVERY desk where space is visible (desk=* in their state.txt, owner 2026-10-27); 0 = only on the bridge desk, the old behaviour | 1
TUNE | rock_vpc       | 4     | voxels per cell edge of an asteroid or a resource node (4 = each rock cube is 4 x 4 x 4 voxels showing the whole rock tile, like the skiff; 1 = the old coarse lump)                | 4
TUNE | skiff_vpc       | 4     | voxels per cell edge of the other ship (4 = each of its tile cubes is 4 x 4 x 4 voxels showing the whole tile; the ship's own cube size)                      | 4
TUNE | skiff_lift_pct  | 120   | brightness of the other ship's tile colours in percent (160 = the first guess; the skiff read paler than the ship, lower it toward 100 to match)                         | 160
TUNE | skiff_wall      | 3     | how many cubes high the other ship's walls stand on its floor cube (the layout is SK_SKIFF in rpg_space.c, 6 x 6 cells)                                         | 3
TUNE | minimap_margin  | 16    | cells shown around the 16 x 16 desk on the engine minimap (16 = the whole 48 x 48 land, so the camera, ships and asteroids outside the desk are on it; 0 = desk only)    | 16
TUNE | minimap_follow  | 0     | 1 = the minimap shows only a minimap_view-cell window that follows the camera (clamped to the land), for a small minimap on a big map; 0 = the whole area at once    | 0
TUNE | minimap_view    | 24    | cells across the following minimap window                                                                                                                              | 24
TUNE | minimap_max_px  | 240   | the minimap's size in pixels, its largest side (the engine scales it down on a small window)                                                                           | 240
TUNE | world_ambient   | 1     | 1 = with the helm off and a planet below, keep the land entity (and the objects over their own planet) drawn in every ship room, at altitude 1; 0 = only while flying direct (the old behaviour)                  | 1
TUNE | gen_vox_max     | 1024  | the most voxels a generated / user asteroid model (asteroids/<name>/model.txt) may have; more are ignored                                                            | 1024
